    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0355" n="239" xml:id="pg239"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/513.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-12-08">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">December</hi> 8, 1911</date>. (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received Dec. 9</hi>.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The veterans now demand dismissal of “traitors” from judiciary and elective
                    offices as well as from the civil service. Bill to suspend the civil service
                        law<anchor n="1" xml:id="d326-f1"/> has passed the House and will probably
                    pass the Senate to-day.</p>
                <p>The Speaker, Ferrara, in answering the argument that the bill was contrary to the
                    Platt amendment, claimed that as Cuba had adopted the amendment under coercion
                    it was not binding upon her.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
